{'review': '{\n  "review": {\n    "overall_status": "NEEDS_FIXES",\n    "quality_score": 6.5,\n    "summary": {\n      "critical": 0,\n      "high": 2,\n      "medium": 1,\n      "low": 0,\n      "passed_checks": [\n        "Type annotations",\n        "No hardcoded secrets",\n        "Proper error handling with unknown",\n        "Use of useMemo for sorting",\n        "Use of useCallback to prevent re-renders"\n      ]\n    },\n    "findings": [\n      {\n        "finding_id": "F-001",\n        "severity": "high",\n        "category": "quality",\n        "title": "Risk of setting state on unmounted component in fetchTodos and getTodo",\n        "file": "src/hooks/useTodos.ts",\n        "line_range": [20, 38],\n        "description": "In fetchTodos and getTodo functions, state (loading, error, todos) is set after asynchronous operations without checking if the component is still mounted. This can cause memory leaks and React warnings.",\n        "impact": "Setting state on unmounted component leads to memory leaks and console warnings in development.",\n        "suggested_fix": "Add a mounted ref to track component state and check it before setting state. Alternatively, use AbortController to cancel requests on unmount.",\n        "code_before": "  const fetchTodos = useCallback(async () => {\\n    setLoading(true);\\n    setError(null);\\n    try {\\n      let completedFilter: boolean | undefined;\\n      if (filter === \'active\') {\\n        completedFilter = false;\\n      } else if (filter === \'completed\') {\\n        completedFilter = true;\\n      }\\n      const data = await getTodos(completedFilter);\\n      setTodos(data);\\n    } catch (err: unknown) {\\n      if (err instanceof Error) {\\n        setError(err.message);\\n      } else {\\n        setError(\'An unknown error occurred during todo operation.\');\\n      }\\n    } finally {\\n      setLoading(false);\\n    }\\n  }, [filter]);",\n        "code_after": "  const fetchTodos = useCallback(async () => {\\n    setLoading(true);\\n    setError(null);\\n    try {\\n      let completedFilter: boolean | undefined;\\n      if (filter === \'active\') {\\n        completedFilter = false;\\n      } else if (filter === \'completed\') {\\n        completedFilter = true;\\n      }\\n      const data = await getTodos(completedFilter);\\n      if (mountedRef.current) {\\n        setTodos(data);\\n      }\\n    } catch (err: unknown) {\\n      if (err instanceof Error) {\\n        if (mountedRef.current) {\\n          setError(err.message);\\n        }\\n      } else {\\n        if (mountedRef.current) {\\n          setError(\'An unknown error occurred during todo operation.\');\\n        }\\n      }\\n    } finally {\\n      if (mountedRef.current) {\\n        setLoading(false);\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }, [filter]);\\n\\n  // Add at top of hook:\\n  // const mountedRef = useRef(true);\\n  // useEffect(() => {\\n  //   return () => {\\n  //     mountedRef.current = false;\\n  //   };\\n  // }, []);",\n        "references": [\n          "https://reactjs.org/docs/state-and-lifecycle.html#cleaning-up",\n          "https://overreacted.io/why-do-we-write-returned-callbacks-so-much/"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        "finding_id": "F-002",\n        "severity": "high",\n        "category": "quality",\n        "title": "Missing cleanup of AbortController leading to potential memory leaks and race conditions",\n        "file": "src/hooks/useTodos.ts",\n        "line_range": [20, 42],\n        "description": "The fetchTodos function does not cancel previous requests when filter changes rapidly, risking race conditions where stale responses overwrite newer data. Additionally, AbortController instances are not cleaned up, causing memory leaks.",\n        "impact": "Stale API responses may incorrectly update state, showing outdated todos. Unaborted fetch requests consume memory and may cause unexpected behavior.",\n        "suggested_fix": "Implement AbortController to cancel previous requests before starting new ones and clean up on unmount or filter change.",\n        "code_before": "  const fetchTodos = useCallback(async () => {\\n    setLoading(true);\\n    setError(null);\\n    try {\\n      let completedFilter: boolean | undefined;\\n      if (filter === \'active\') {\\n        completedFilter = false;\\n      } else if (filter === \'completed\') {\\n        completedFilter = true;\\n      }\\n      const data = await getTodos(completedFilter);\\n      setTodos(data);\\n    } catch (err: unknown) {\\n      if (err instanceof Error) {\\n        setError(err.message);\\n      } else {\\n        setError(\'An unknown error occurred during todo operation.\');\\n      }\\n    } finally {\\n      setLoading(false);\\n    }\\n  }, [filter]);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    fetchTodos();\\n  }, [fetchTodos]);",\n        "code_after": "  const fetchTodos = useCallback(async () => {\\n    // Cancel any ongoing request\\n    if (abortControllerRef.current) {\\n      abortControllerRef.current.abort();\\n    }\\n    setLoading(true);\\n    setError(null);\\n    const abortController = new AbortController();\\n    abortControllerRef.current = abortController;\\n    try {\\n      let completedFilter: boolean | undefined;\\n      if (filter === \'active\') {\\n        completedFilter = false;\\n      } else if (filter === \'completed\') {\\n        completedFilter = true;\\n      }\\n      const data = await getTodos(completedFilter, { signal: abortController.signal });\\n      if (mountedRef.current) {\\n        setTodos(data);\\n      }\\n    } catch (err: unknown) {\\n      if (err instanceof Error && err.name !== \'AbortError\') {\\n        if (mountedRef.current) {\\n          if (err instanceof Error) {\\n            setError(err.message);\\n          } else {\\n            setError(\'An unknown error occurred during todo operation.\');\\n          }\\n        }\\n      }\\n      // Ignore abort errors\\n    } finally {\\n      if (mountedRef.current) {\\n        setLoading(false);\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }, [filter]);\\n\\n  useEffect(() => {\\n    fetchTodos();\\n  }, [fetchTodos]);\\n\\n  // Add at top of hook:\\n  // const abortControllerRef = useRef(null);\\n  // const mountedRef = useRef(true);\\n  // useEffect(() => {\\n  //   return () => {\\n  //     mountedRef.current = false;\\n  //     if (abortControllerRef.current) {\\n  //       abortControllerRef.current.abort();\\n  //     }\\n  //   };\\n  // }, []);",\n        "references": [\n          "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/AbortController",\n          "https://reactjs.org/docs/hooks-effect.html#example-using-hooks-1"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        "finding_id": "F-003",\n        "severity": "medium",\n        "category": "quality",\n        "title": "Optimistic state update in updateExistingTodo may mismatch backend state",\n        "file": "src/hooks/useTodos.ts",\n        "line_range": [50, 70],\n        "description": "The updateExistingTodo function updates todos state with payload data immediately after API call, assuming backend returns identical data. If backend transforms data (e.g., trimming whitespace normalization, case conversion) or ignores fields, UI state becomes inconsistent with server.",\n        "impact": "UI may display incorrect todo data after update, leading to user confusion and potential data loss if user relies on outdated UI state.",\n        "suggested_fix": "Refetch the updated todo or entire list after successful update to ensure state consistency with backend.",\n        "code_before": "    await updateTodo(id, payload);\\n    setTodos((prev) => prev.map((todo) => (todo.id === id ? { ...todo, ...payload } as Todo : todo)));",\n        "code_after": "    await updateTodo(id, payload);\\n    // Refetch updated todo to ensure consistency\\n    const updatedTodo = await getTodoById(id);\\n    setTodos((prev) => prev.map((todo) => (todo.id === id ? updatedTodo : todo)));\\n    // Alternative: refetch entire list (less efficient)\\n    // await fetchTodos();",\n        "references": []\n      }\n    ],\n    "positive_observations": [\n      "Strong TypeScript usage with proper generics and type safety",\n      "No hardcoded secrets or credentials in client-side code",\n      "Error handling correctly distinguishes Error instances from unknown values",\n      "Effective use of useMemo to prevent expensive recalculations of sorted todos",\n      "Appropriate use of useCallback to prevent unnecessary function re-creations",\n      "Loading and error states properly managed for asynchronous operations"\n    ]\n  }\n}'}